        "subject": "LU-20426 lnet: netlink interface for stats commands",
        "message": "LU-20426 lnet: netlink interface for stats commands\n\nThe \"lnetctl stats show\" and \"lnetctl stats reset\" commands are the\nlast LNet statistics paths still carried over ioctl, while net, peer\nand route already moved to the Netlink generic interface. Their fixed\nioctl structures cannot grow a field without breaking the ABI, which\nleaves no room to add statistics controls.\n\nAdd an LNET_CMD_STATS Netlink command. A dump returns the global LNet\ncounters as a schema-tagged statistics mapping, rendered by name in\nuserspace, and a doit resets them. lnetctl issues the Netlink request\nfirst and falls back to the existing ioctl when the running module\ndoes not provide the command, so a newer lnetctl still drives an older\nmodule.\n\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4.8\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I8ddf2c9c32fa99b8b8d1087816e3875ab9fe8e1e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
